course: dictionary
lesson: 21
title: Absence: being away, or not there
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Absence is a noun. It means being away from a place where you should be, or a time when someone is away. The words around it give the clue: «Too many absences from school can be a problem.» The word school tells you absences must mean times away from school.
explain: Absence can also mean that something is not there at all. «In the absence of light, plants cannot make food.» If there is no light, plants cannot make food. Try your meaning in the sentence: without light, plants cannot make food. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Look for the phrases too. In the absence of means without, or when something is missing. Absence from school and a long absence are phrases you will see in registers, letters and reports.
fact: Absence means being away from a place where you should be.
fact: «Absences» is the plural, so it means more than one absence.
fact: «In the absence of» means without, or when something is not there.
fact: Schools take a register every day, and absences are recorded in it.
fact: In maths about attendance, present = total − absent: if 3 pupils are absent from a class of 28, then 25 are present.
exercise: «Too many absences from school can be a problem.» What does absences mean here? | Pupils who are very tall | *Times when someone is away | Lessons that are fun | Books in the library
exercise: «In the absence of light, plants cannot make food.» What does in the absence of light mean? | Light that is green | Very bright light | Light from a torch only | *Without any light
exercise: A class has 28 pupils. The register shows 3 absences today. How many pupils are present? | 31 | *25 | 3 | 28
test: «Leo had a long absence from school.» What does a long absence mean? | *Being away for a long time | A long pencil with a sharp tip | Winning a prize at school | Being at school all day
test: Which phrase means without or when something is missing? | Long absence | Absence from school | *In the absence of | Leave of absence
exam: Which sentence uses absence correctly? | Absence is the colour of the sky. | The absence ran fast across the field. | *Ravi's absence from school was noted in the register. | Absence is a bright red bicycle.
